# BizToolLab project strategy

`docs/PROJECT_STRATEGY.md` is the authoritative business and production strategy. Consult it when planning significant work, modifying code, assessing production impact, or preparing releases. Follow it. Do not copy or replace it.

BizToolLab, a product of Synergy Media & Tech LLC, is an existing live production website. Local work is not deployed until a separate, authorized release.

Keep the ongoing Google Search Console traffic-testing initiative visible in sprint planning. Preserve measurement integrity. Do not invent Search Console metrics or assume access to live data.

SEO, AdSense readiness, and sustainable revenue generation remain permanent considerations even when they are not the sprint focus. If a sprint has no direct SEO or monetization impact, say so.

Consider both workstreams on significant work. Do not abandon either silently:

- Product Engineering: build, test, secure, and improve the platform.
- Traffic and Revenue Readiness: organic visibility, public value, growth, and monetization readiness.

Protect existing public URLs, calculators, content, functionality, indexing, and user experience.

Treat implementation, tests, commits, pushes, database migrations, and production deployments as distinct operations. Never push or deploy without explicit user authorization. Never execute a live database migration without explicit authorization.

For relevant changes, identify potential production, indexing, and measurement consequences before release. This rule supplements existing engineering instructions, architecture, testing practices, and security requirements. It does not replace them.
